/** @dir Lib/MakeASound/Audio
    Audio buffers and the processing interface (namespace MakeASound), with no
    device behind them; part of MakeASoundCore.

    - Buffer is a planar float block that owns or refers to memory; Channel and
      ConstChannel are views of one channel. Slicing by samples or channels
      never allocates.
    - Processor is the unit of audio work that Engine and every plugin format
      run. It declares its buses (BusLayout), is prepared with a ProcessSpec
      and handed a ProcessContext each block, with the Playhead when a host
      has one.
    - process() runs on the audio thread: no allocation, locks or logging.
*/
